SUMMARY:Twenty Years of Valcour Records
LOCATION:Acadiana Center for the Arts - James Devin Moncus Theater\, 101 W.
  Vermilion Street
DESCRIPTION:This show has sold out\, but you can still watch the concert on
 line! Join our waitlist to be notified if any seats open up prior to the c
 oncert. For two decades\, Valcour Records has stood at the heart of Louisi
 ana’s roots renaissance — preserving the traditions of Cajun\, Creole\
 , zydeco\, and folk while amplifying the voices shaping its future. Founde
 d in Eunice\, Louisiana\, by partners Joel Savoy and Phillip LaFargue\, Va
 lcour has become a touchstone for the state’s cultural identity\, produc
 ing award-winning albums and nurturing artists whose music carries the sou
 nd and soul of Acadiana to audiences around the world. This special Louisi
 ana Crossroads concert brings together the label’s musicians and collabo
 rators for an evening that honors Valcour’s 20-year journey. Through liv
 e collaborations and stories\, this evening traces the label’s evolution
  from a group of friends recording in Savoy’s living room\, to a nationa
 lly respected imprint.   C.J. Chenier T’Monde Pine Leaf Boys The Band C
 ourtbouillon featuring Wayne Toups Caleb Klauder and Reeb Willms Sammy Lin
 d and Nadine Landry Joel Savoy Kyle Huval K. C. Jones Jesse Lege Johnny Ni
 cholas Katie Shore Ann Savoy Jane Vidrine The Mamou Playboys Jourdan Thibo
 deaux Blake Miller Bonsoir Catin Josh Caffery Roger Kash Sabra Guzman Boma
  Bango Tif Lamson\n\nhttps://acadianacenterforthearts.org/events/twenty-ye
 ars-of-valcour-records/?occurrence=2026-11-19
